    "result": "Perfect! The fix is complete and tested. Here's a summary of what was fixed:\n\n## Bug Fix Summary\n\n**Problem:** The `frai gate init --ci` command through the CLI wasn't creating the `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` file, even though the direct `frai-gate init --ci` command did.\n\n**Root Cause:** The `gate` command handler in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` was only passing positional arguments to the delegated `frai-gate` CLI, not the command-line options like `--ci`. Commander.js parses options separately from positional arguments, and the original code wasn't capturing them.\n\n**Solution:** Modified the gate command handler to:\n1. Remove parameter capture from Commander's action handler (which doesn't properly expose unknown options)\n2. Access `process.argv` directly to find all arguments after 'gate'\n3. Pass the complete argument list (including flags) to the `frai-gate` CLI\n\n**Verification:** After rebuilding with `pnpm --filter frai build`, the command now correctly creates both:\n- `FRAI-SPEC.md` - the AI gate specification template\n- `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` - the GitHub Actions workflow that runs the gate on every PR",
